        "original_id": "e4489063-39fd-527e-a5ba-177a0ec5c567",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Cairo Junction, Illinois; Streatorland; Cairo; Illinois River\n- Roads: U.S. Route 51; Illinois Route 3; Illinois Route 37; Interstate 39; Interstate 55\n- Topics: highway location; route extent; highway replacement; regional boundaries\n\nFacts:\n- U.S. Route 51 is a south-north United States highway that runs 1,286 miles from the western suburbs of New Orleans, Louisiana, to within 100 feet of the Wisconsin–Michigan border.\n- In the early 1980s, U.S. Route 51 was one of the busiest two-lane highways in the United States.\n- Interstate 39 was designed to replace U.S. Route 51.\n- Cairo Junction, Illinois, is located at the junction of U.S. Route 51, Illinois Route 3, and Illinois Route 37 north of Cairo.\n- Streatorland can be more broadly defined as the area east of Interstate 39, west of Interstate 55, and south of the Illinois River.",
